<Placemark><name>Nichols Arboretum (the Arb)</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[If it's a really nice day and you have time. It's right next to the Hill dorms, so it's an easy add-on to that detour: from Observatory St, walk east to the end of Washington Heights and you're at the edge of the Arb. The trails head down to the Huron River.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.72238,42.27908,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>North Campus (engineering)</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[If Will is considering engineering, you need to go up to North Campus. It's a drive or a U-M bus from Central Campus, not part of the walk. Worth seeing: Lurie Tower (this pin), the Duderstadt Center next door, and the Wave Field.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.71618,42.29203,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
